\ parse.fth - 4000 lines of interpreted arithmetic. No definitions, no
\ loops: almost all of the time is the outer interpreter - parsing a
\ line, finding each word in the dictionary, converting each number.
\ It is here because corpus-run.sh and loop-bench.sh disagreed about
\ which family is faster, and this is the workload that says why.
